    delphi:hasScore "0.838"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.87"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Counts and species identity are direct variables, and public specimen imagery can yield large samples. The named examples and constancy criterion provide clear confirming and refuting outcomes." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Count opposing parastichy families in many georeferenced cones per conifer species and estimate within-species frequency distributions, explicitly checking the stated 5/3 spruce and 8/5 larch modes. Tight species-specific modes support the claim; broad variation or different dominant counts refutes it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Images must show the cone at sufficient resolution and orientation.", "Cultivar, age and cone position may contribute within-species variation." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch14-04--gpt--dataset-1> .
